<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The light gene (built 2026-09-30, CASTES-PLAN.md phase 1). Carrying it makes
		a mamono giddy in man-made light and a little muddled by it. The mothman is
		the caste it was written for and the only one carrying it.

		IMPORTANT, and it bit for a few days (fixed 2026-10-04): the mood half is a
		thought whose worker is asked about EVERY PAWN on the map, carrier or not,
		because a non-social situational thought is collected from the whole
		thought database per pawn (`SituationalThoughtHandler.UpdateAllMoodThoughts`
		over `ThoughtUtility.situationalNonSocialThoughtDefs`). So a new thought
		worker here must answer `Inactive` for a pawn who does not carry its gene
		first, and only then read the condition. See
		`ThoughtWorker_DisorientatingLights` in Source/Insects/DisorientatingLights.cs.

		The rule, decided 2026-09-30: -5% consciousness and +10 mood while she
		stands in artificial light at exactly 50% - the value a man-made light
		source gives - and NOT under a growing lamp, whose bright core is a
		different value. A glowing cave counts as light.

		All of that is one engine number and no def names anywhere. `GlowGrid`
		(Verse/GlowGrid.cs) caps ordinary light sources at 0.5
		(MaxGameGlowFromNonOverlitGroundLights) and returns a flat 1.0 on every cell
		inside a source's `overlightRadius` (AlphaOfOverlit). A vanilla
		`StandingLamp` has no overlight radius, so it reads 0.5; the vanilla
		`SunLamp` - the growing lamp - has `overlightRadius 7.0`, so its bright core
		reads 1.0 and is the one place the gene does not fire.
		Source/Insects/DisorientatingLights.cs holds the test and both halves.

		Two halves, two homes, and that is the interesting part of this gene. A
		hediff cannot carry the mood: `HediffStage` has `overrideMoodBase`, which
		REPLACES the mood base rather than adding to it. So the consciousness
		penalty is the hidden hediff `PMM_Hediff_DisorientatingLights`, which the
		gene class adds and removes as the light changes, and the mood is the
		thought `PMM_Thought_DisorientatingLights`.

		Displayed lines: none, on purpose. The gene carries no stat offsets and no
		abilities, so the engine prints nothing for it, and the hidden hediff is
		invisible on the Health tab. That is why the description below states the
		two numbers itself: there is no effect line for them to live in.
	-->
	<GeneDef>
		<defName>PMM_Gene_DisorientatingLights</defName>
		<label>disorientating lights</label>
		<description>A moth's eyes: a lamp is a pleasure and a puzzle at once. While she stands in a man-made light - a lamp, a torch, a fire, a glowing cave - she is giddy and her mind swims, worth 10 mood and costing her 5% of her consciousness. The bright core of a growing lamp is the one light that does nothing for her.</description>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_DisorientatingLights</iconPath>
		<geneClass>PMM_Insects.Gene_DisorientatingLights</geneClass>
		<displayCategory>Miscellaneous</displayCategory>
		<displayOrderInCategory>1002</displayOrderInCategory>
		<!-- Complexity 1, and out of the random gene sets (2026-10-01): priced with
		     the vanilla drawback, and not something a trader's genepack should hand to a
		     stranger - Genes_Insect.xml carries the mechanism in full. -->
		<biostatCpx>1</biostatCpx>
		<canGenerateInGeneSet>false</canGenerateInGeneSet>
		<!-- No metabolic cost, and that is the ruling rather than an oversight: the light
		     does the work, and the price she pays is the muddled head it comes with. -->
		<biostatMet>0</biostatMet>
	</GeneDef>

</Defs>
